155745, PubMed:15985469). Inhibits mitochondrial fusion by creating a non-fusogenic lipid environment which affects OPA1 oligomerization and its subsequent capacity to drive fusion (PubMed:38851188). This prevents defective inner mitochondrial membrane (IMM) subdomains from fusing with other mitochondria, facilitating their segregation into small MTFP1-enriched mitochondria (SMEM) which are targeted for autophagic degradation (PubMed:38851188, PubMed:41398051). This IMM quality control mechanism controls mitochondrial DNA levels (PubMed:38851188)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}